# Normalise every text file to LF in the repository and in the working tree.
#
# This is not cosmetic. skills/herdr-cron/**.md is compiled into the binary with
# //go:embed, and `herdr-cron --skill` promises to print bytes identical to the
# file on disk (docs/spec/08-agent-skill.md §2). A Windows checkout with the
# default core.autocrlf would embed CRLF, so the same tag would ship a different
# skill on different platforms — and the frontmatter parser, which anchors on
# "---\n", would stop recognising its own document. That is exactly how the
# first Windows CI run failed.
#
# It also keeps the .editorconfig `end_of_line = lf` rule true rather than
# aspirational, and keeps `gofmt -l` from flagging a whole tree on Windows.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, never touched.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.gz binary
*.zip binary
